\ The first gate positions, with zero anchored at Foundation.
\ The positive gap is 345, the negative gap is 503.
\ These values came from independent full-sauce calculations.
\ This does not test arbitrarily distant gate positions.

To check the first signed gate positions:
  Locate a gate given 0.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "Gate zero did not stay at Foundation." into the check report; exit.
  Locate a gate given 1.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055326,
    put "Gate 1 was not 345 days after Foundation." into the check report; exit.
  Locate a gate given -1.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15056174,
    put "Gate -1 was not 503 days before Foundation." into the check report; exit.


\ Verify the ownership of a gap when moving across gate zero.
\ Gap at negative gate -1 is 503 days; positive gap +1 is 345.
\ These four single steps must never request a gap for index zero.
To check gate zero crossings:
  Put -1 into the gate walk's current index.
  Put -15056174 into the gate walk's current position.
  Move to the next positive gate.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "Crossing from gate -1 ended at the wrong index." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "Crossing from gate -1 to zero used the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
  Move to the next positive gate.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055326,
    put "Crossing from gate zero to +1 used the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
  Move to the next negative gate.
  If the gate walk's current index is not 0,
    put "Returning from gate +1 ended at the wrong index." into the check report; exit.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15055671,
    put "Returning from gate +1 to zero used the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
  Move to the next negative gate.
  If the gate walk's current position is not -15056174,
    put "Returning from gate zero to -1 used the wrong gap." into the check report; exit.
